    "text": "18 ITERATIVE IMPORTANCE SAMPLING WITH MARKOV CHAIN MONTE CARLO SAMPLING \n\nAppendix C. Proof of existence of minimum \n\nTo guarantee the minimum exist in our example, it is enough to prove that the expectation is continuous as a function of ( _µ_ 0 _, τ_ 0) on [ _−_ 8 _,_ 68] _×_ [5 _,_ 16]. \n\nBy Fubini’s theorem in our example, we have \n\n\n\nwhere \n\n\n\nis the posterior probability distribution. The proportionality constant _c_ ( _µ_ 0 _, τ_ 0) is given by \n\n\n\nwhere \n\n\n\nSince _a_ ( _τµ, k, µ_ 0) _>_ 0, then by Lemma D.1 in (48), we get that the integral with respect to _µ_ is \n\n\n\nNote that _a_ ( _τµ, k, µ_ 0), _b_ ( _τµ, k, µ_ 0) and _c_ ( _τµ, k, µ_ 0) are continuously differentiable and _τµ ∈_ [1 _, τ_ 0] and _k ∈_ [1 _,_ 5]. Thus, by Leibniz integral rule it follows that _c_ ( _µ_ 0 _, τ_ 0) is continuously differentiable on [ _−_ 8 _,_ 68] _×_ [5 _,_ 16]. \n\n"
